    "class": "gps-587506166926475946 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/c80c08-d3/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_STATIC&editorId=587506166808969898&sectionId=587506166926475946)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggkMWLdujeH_text","label":"ggkMWLdujeH_text","default":"Pawsome Prime Sale - Free Gift With Purchase"},{"type":"html","id":"ggzl_PTQ3ut_text","label":"ggzl_PTQ3ut_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:rgb(255,22,22);font-size:inherit;\">Think Your Dog’s Eyes Are Safe?&nbsp;</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggttme0GmRQ_text","label":"ggttme0GmRQ_text","default":"<p>Think Again - They’re&nbsp;</p><p>in Mortal Peril</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3jGbiHqd7_text","label":"gg3jGbiHqd7_text","default":"<p>Your dog’s eyes may seem fine now, but below the surface…</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Big trouble is brewing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Dirt, discharge, and allergens are constantly building up</strong>,</span> creating the perfect storm for irritation, infections, and even irreversible damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Many pet owners don’t realize that the area around their dog’s eyes is one of the most vulnerable parts of their body. Without regular, thorough cleaning, bacteria and grime can silently cause inflammation, redness, and painful infections.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Left untreated, these issues can spiral into severe complications…</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>And even blindness.</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggVGL3N63NF_text","label":"ggVGL3N63NF_text","default":"<p>Here’s the scary truth:</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggsalRS_G8f_text","label":"ggsalRS_G8f_text","default":"<p>Basic cleaning methods like tissues, cotton balls, or baby wipes aren’t just ineffective, they’re dangerous</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjf4cJi083_text","label":"ggjf4cJi083_text","default":"<p>Cotton Balls</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggUVJocpju2_text","label":"ggUVJocpju2_text","default":"<p>Tissues</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gggvMLMQdKr_text","label":"gggvMLMQdKr_text","default":"<p>Baby wipes</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg8xWejiQ3K_text","label":"gg8xWejiQ3K_text","default":"<p><strong>Using the wrong tools can spread bacteria, cause irritation, and make the problem worse.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Most dogs won’t show signs of eye discomfort until the situation is critical - when they’re already scratching, squinting, or pawing at their face in pain. By then, the damage could be done, and your beloved pet could be facing a costly vet visit or worse.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This isn’t a risk you want to take.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Your dog’s vision depends on proper care, and without it, the consequences could be devastating.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggqhjSAjyjN_text","label":"ggqhjSAjyjN_text","default":"<p>Redness</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggsxPOWrBIe_text","label":"ggsxPOWrBIe_text","default":"<p>Inflammation</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrcJXYuery_text","label":"ggrcJXYuery_text","default":"<p>Swelling</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggmj658sQKM_text","label":"ggmj658sQKM_text","default":"<p>Eye Discharge</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3BQ3_78V0_text","label":"gg3BQ3_78V0_text","default":"<p>Blood Under Cornea</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggkJkLKLOdA_text","label":"ggkJkLKLOdA_text","default":"<p>Small Pupil</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg9vGD4nSXa_text","label":"gg9vGD4nSXa_text","default":"<p>Redness</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggVCUwyP7hK_text","label":"ggVCUwyP7hK_text","default":"<p>Inflammation</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggX5lOkAbfV_text","label":"ggX5lOkAbfV_text","default":"<p>Swelling</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg5_PbqdOR5_text","label":"gg5_PbqdOR5_text","default":"<p>Eye Discharge</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggkHB02q1iR_text","label":"ggkHB02q1iR_text","default":"<p>Small Pupil</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggtkuLsdkvl_text","label":"ggtkuLsdkvl_text","default":"<p>How Mild Discharge Can Lead to Permanent Blindness</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg293uY8oAH_text","label":"gg293uY8oAH_text","default":"<p>It might seem harmless: just a little discharge around your dog’s eyes. But here’s the terrifying truth: <strong>what starts as mild irritation can spiral into irreversible damage.</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg-kvJ35k7K_text","label":"gg-kvJ35k7K_text","default":"<p>When dirt and bacteria build up around your pet’s eyes, they don’t just cause minor redness or discomfort. This buildup can quickly lead to serious infections that damage the cornea, block tear ducts, and even spread to the delicate internal structures of the eye.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggNNgwzzzOf_text","label":"ggNNgwzzzOf_text","default":"<p>And once the damage is done, it can’t always be undone.&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggBG-b7anN2_text","label":"ggBG-b7anN2_text","default":"<p>If left untreated, these infections can escalate rapidly.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggWEzsZ2GMH_text","label":"ggWEzsZ2GMH_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(223,231,253);color:rgb(48,48,48);font-size:18px;\">According to the <strong>American Veterinary Medical Associatio</strong>n, complications like <strong>corneal ulcers or uveitis (severe inflammation inside the eye</strong>) can result from untreated infections.&nbsp;</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggqKNuMrDV2_text","label":"ggqKNuMrDV2_text","default":"<p>These conditions are not only excruciatingly painful but also <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>frequent precursors&nbsp;</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>to permanent vision loss.</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg5lVHDS_40_text","label":"gg5lVHDS_40_text","default":"<p>And the scariest part?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Most dogs won’t show signs of a problem until it’s too late.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dogs instinctively hide their pain. By the time you notice symptoms like squinting, excessive tearing, or greenish-yellow discharge, the infection has likely advanced to&nbsp;a critical stage.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Without swift intervention, <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>blindness becomes a very real possibility.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Elvira</strong></span>, a doting furmom to her <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Rottweiler</strong>, <strong>Damian</strong></span>, this nightmare became all&nbsp;too real…</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggE8otnUdt5_text","label":"ggE8otnUdt5_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(48,48,48);font-size:18px;\">The fateful day Damian faced the crushing consequences of unchecked eye issues.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIpZZFT_-v_text","label":"ggIpZZFT_-v_text","default":"How Ignoring Discharge Nearly Cost&nbsp;<br>Damian His Vision"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfJuRgD5bs_text","label":"ggfJuRgD5bs_text","default":"<p>Elvira and her Rottweiler, Damian, were a team. As an avid marathon runner, Elvira trained almost every day, and Damian was always by her side. They loved their evening runs through the city after work - Damian trotting beside her, soaking up the sights and smells.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggxGpWEPTBB_text","label":"ggxGpWEPTBB_text","default":"<p>But the city wasn’t just filled with interesting scents and sounds. <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Every step they took was kicking up dirt, dust, and debris</strong>,</span> and without Elvira realizing it, Damian’s eyes were&nbsp;</p><p>paying the price.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggwhSgsX1rD_text","label":"ggwhSgsX1rD_text","default":"<p>At first, it seemed harmless. <strong>Occasional watery discharge or a little eye gunk after their runs </strong>- she figured it was normal. She’d wipe it away with tissues or a basic pet wipe, sure she was doing everything Damian needed.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCvroNtXBw_text","label":"ggCvroNtXBw_text","default":"<p>Elvira and her Rottweiler, Damian, were a team. As an avid marathon runner, Elvira trained almost every day, and Damian was always by her side. They loved their evening runs through the city after work - Damian trotting beside her, soaking up the sights and smells.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg_6p78e79l_text","label":"gg_6p78e79l_text","default":"<p>But the city wasn’t just filled with interesting scents and sounds. <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Every step they took was kicking up dirt, dust, and debris</strong>,</span> and without Elvira realizing it, Damian’s eyes were&nbsp;</p><p>paying the price.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggU1M8TBZXi_text","label":"ggU1M8TBZXi_text","default":"<p>At first, it seemed harmless. Occasional watery discharge or a little eye gunk after their runs - she figured it was normal. She’d wipe it away with tissues or a basic pet wipe, sure she was doing everything Damian needed.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2BIzrfMLP_text","label":"gg2BIzrfMLP_text","default":"<p>But Things Took Turn For The Worse</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggAJtV6R6NY_text","label":"ggAJtV6R6NY_text","default":"<p>At first, the signs were subtle - barely noticeable, even. Damian blinked a little more often, and Elvira noticed his eyes watering on windy days. She dismissed it as irritation from city smog or something Damian sniffed while on their runs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But then, the symptoms worsened. <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Redness appeared in the whites of his eyes</strong></span>, and the watery discharge thickened into yellowish gunk that stuck to the corners.&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg-PTho27Oa_text","label":"gg-PTho27Oa_text","default":"<p>Damian began pawing at his face and squinting in discomfort. He flinched when she tried to clean his eyes, and eventually, he didn’t even want to head out for their nightly runs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>Elvira was heartbroken. Damian wasn’t just her running partner - he was her best friend.&nbsp;</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>She rushed him to the vet, terrified of what she might hear.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gghg5fgE5MN_text","label":"gghg5fgE5MN_text","default":"<p>Damian Was Suffering Without Elvira Realizing It</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg0Yyx9gmgG_text","label":"gg0Yyx9gmgG_text","default":"<p>Replace this text The vet’s diagnosis hit her like a punch to the gut.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A<span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"> <strong>severe eye infection</strong></span> had taken hold, caused by dirt and bacteria building up around Damian’s eyes after their runs. Worse, the vet explained that her efforts to clean his eyes with tissues and general wipes had likely pushed bacteria further into delicate areas, making things worse instead of better.&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggUiIfsUxu9_text","label":"ggUiIfsUxu9_text","default":"<p><i>The vet didn’t mince words:&nbsp;</i></p><p><span style=\"color:#E81313;font-size:21px;\">“If you hadn’t brought him in today, Damian could &nbsp;have lost his vision.”</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggLUIF9KbhI_text","label":"ggLUIF9KbhI_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(48,48,48);font-size:18px;\">Elvira sat stunned as the vet outlined the long road ahead - antibiotics, prescription eye drops, and weeks of close monitoring to ensure the infection didn’t spread further. She had tried so hard to take care of Damian, but this silent problem had been growing unnoticed.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg90nggVPV5_text","label":"gg90nggVPV5_text","default":"<p>Elvira’s Attempts To Help Almost Cost Damian His Sight</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfxntIjRXm_text","label":"ggfxntIjRXm_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(48,48,48);font-size:18px;\">Elvira felt an overwhelming wave of guilt. She’d done what she thought was best, <strong>but the wrong tools had allowed bacteria to thrive,</strong> turning a minor issue into a crisis.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg7oxe3JNz9_text","label":"gg7oxe3JNz9_text","default":"<p>She vowed never to let it happen again. Regular cleaning with the <span style=\"font-size:inherit;\"><strong>right products designed specifically for sensitive eyes</strong></span> wasn’t just a suggestion - it was essential.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Determined to protect Damian and keep him healthy, Elvira began searching for a better way to care for his eyes…</p>"}],
    "blocks": [{"type": "@app"}],
    "locales": {}
